  <Docs>
    <summary>Controls tunnels established via HTTP CONNECT.</summary>
    <remarks>
      <para>Controls tunnels established via HTTP CONNECT. All methods will be invoked onto the Executor specified in Proxy.createHttpProxy(int, String, int, Executor, HttpConnectCallback).</para>
      <para>Methods within this class are invoked only when HttpEngine must establish a tunnel through the proxy. Refer to Proxy.createHttpProxy(int, String, int, Executor, HttpConnectCallback)'s documentation to understand when that is the case.</para>
      <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/net/http/Proxy.HttpConnectCallback" title="Reference documentation">Android reference for <code>android.net.http.Proxy.HttpConnectCallback</code>.</a></format></para>
